    "explanation": "To both parties: the $4.50 cancellation fee is neither collected nor refunded today. It is placed on hold and the case goes to a human reviewer, because POL-NS-09(c) applies. The two profile snapshots each record 2 disputes with the counterparty in the last 90 days (rider_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d = 2 and driver_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d = 2). Those are exactly the two fields POL-NS-09(c) reads, and together they show 2 disputes between this same rider and this same driver — meeting the clause's '2 or more' threshold. Escalation under POL-NS-09 is terminal, so no monetary ruling issues and the $4.50 stays frozen. The open question the reviewer must settle is whether those two counters do concern disputes between this rider and this driver, and if so whether the pair's history changes the outcome; the snapshots do not itemise them.\n\nSo the reviewer has the merits as well: on the driving evidence the driver made out the baseline no-show. The trip record shows the 'arrived' event at 11:00:27, the 180-second free-waiting period starting at 11:00:29, and cancellation at 11:07:18 under RIDER_NO_SHOW. The GPS trace places him inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius from the arrival timestamp itself (dwell start offset 0.0) and holds him there in one continuous 410-second run to 11:07:17. All four POL-NS-01 conditions therefore hold — arrival event (a), in-geofence at the marker (b), a 410-second dwell against the 180-second minimum with no_show_threshold_sec null (c), no boarding event and a no-show termination after the dwell (d) — and POL-NS-02's three-consecutive-fix test is met 42 times over. No clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces them. On those facts POL-NS-07 would pay the driver 80% of $4.50 = $3.60, its anti-farming guard not tripping (1 no-show termination in 30 days against 86 completed trips is 0.012, below both the count of 4 and the rate of 0.08), and the rider's charge would stand. The escalation displaces that payment, not the findings.\n\nThe rider's routes to a refund fail on the merits. POL-NS-04 does not exonerate her: limbs (a) and (b) may be arguable, but limb (c) is affirmatively failed — her track holds her device 694.4 m to 702.0 m from the pin, stationary at 0.0 km/h at all 79 fixes, with no qualifying fix inside the 100 m STANDARD presence radius — and where limb (c) fails on admissible fixes the clause does not apply and the dispute is decided under POL-NS-01. Her POL-NS-09(b) argument also fails: the message 'coming down now' and the stationary track are not an unresolved contradiction, because POL-NS-04(c) is the clause that reads rider presence and it answers the question; POL-NS-11 covers the case where that test cannot be run, not the case where it runs and fails. POL-NS-03 does not apply, because the stationary fixes lie inside the arrival radius rather than outside it, so the 400 m wrong-entrance route is never reached. POL-NS-05 does not fire against the driver either — he was inside the radius and stationary when he tapped, so no false-arrival referral arises under POL-NS-05(ii) — and POL-NS-06 gives the rider nothing, since its accumulation limb needs more than the single 410-second in-geofence run and the only advisory artifact (EV-ADVIS-03303-01) is MISSING with weight 0.0, relied on for its absence alone.\n\nOn confidence: POL-GEN-02(2) caps confidence at the minimum weight among the artifacts carrying the deciding fact. The artifacts behind every fact above — the trip record, the GPS trace, the fare ledger and both profiles — are COMPLETE at weight 1.0 with no issue codes, so nothing is discounted and no finding needs to survive a discount; the single MISSING advisory at weight 0.0 carries no fact. The money figures used are the $4.50 cancellation fee (fare_breakdown and platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd), the $6.61 gross it may alternatively show, and the $3.60 that POL-NS-07 would have paid. No referral rides with this ruling, because no clause that produces one fires, and POL-GEN-05 is not engaged since no monetary effect issues while the amount is held."
